    "detailed_description": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >LSD: Retro Dream Emulator is a surrealist first-person adventure/walking simulator game about dreams, featuring</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >* trippy, psychedelic visuals</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >* challenging platforms</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >* experimental cosmic horror elements</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >* and last but not least, an overarching feeling of NEVER knowing what to expect.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It explores the idea of a mind losing its grasp with reality, as reality turns into a dream, and that dream turns into a nightmare. It has an off-kilter tone that can shift from overly chill to downright scary. Often it resembles an acid trip, or an interactive fever dream.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A Retro game influenced by the original <strong>LSD: Dream Emulator</strong> from PSX and cosmic horror. Immerse yourself in a dreamy and psychedelic  world through low poly environments and liminal spaces. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game contains gameplay with lots of dreamy scenarios, even more freaky visuals, deconstructed urban landscapes and/or dreamscapes, existential angst, and a bit of horror.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore your deepest thoughts in this game that challenges your mind, between dreams and reality.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Inspired by the art of artists like Moebius, H.P. Lovecraft, Alejandro Jodorowsky, H.R. Giger, and more.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A TOTAL experience.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >LSD: Retro Dream Emulator is a surrealist first-person adventure/walking simulator game about dreams, featuring</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >* trippy, psychedelic visuals</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >* challenging platforms</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >* experimental cosmic horror elements</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >* and last but not least, an overarching feeling of NEVER knowing what to expect.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >It explores the idea of a mind losing its grasp with reality, as reality turns into a dream, and that dream turns into a nightmare. It has an off-kilter tone that can shift from overly chill to downright scary. Often it resembles an acid trip, or an interactive fever dream.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A Retro game influenced by the original <strong>LSD: Dream Emulator</strong> from PSX and cosmic horror. Immerse yourself in a dreamy and psychedelic  world through low poly environments and liminal spaces. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The game contains gameplay with lots of dreamy scenarios, even more freaky visuals, deconstructed urban landscapes and/or dreamscapes, existential angst, and a bit of horror.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Explore your deepest thoughts in this game that challenges your mind, between dreams and reality.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Inspired by the art of artists like Moebius, H.P. Lovecraft, Alejandro Jodorowsky, H.R. Giger, and more.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >A TOTAL experience.</p>",
